.TH FLICK 1 "2026-11-02" "flick 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flick \- search a film or a show, pick a torrent, watch it now
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flick
[\fItitle\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B flick couch
[\fItitle\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B flick
is a full\-screen terminal UI. It opens on a splash, then a wall of posters:
what you were watching and what is trending. Typing searches IMDb. Opening a
title lists torrent sources from YTS, EZTV, The Pirate Bay, Knaben and Nyaa,
with a suggested pick, and pressing enter streams it straight into a player.
Shows get a season and episode list with watched marks and the next episode.
.PP
Films stream through a torrent engine on this computer while they download,
so playback starts in seconds. They are cached, and nothing keeps uploading
once a film is closed.
.PP
Posters are drawn with the kitty graphics protocol in kitty and Ghostty on
macOS. Other terminals show cards with the title instead.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B flick
Open flick: continue watching, trending films and shows, search.
.TP
.B flick \fItitle\fR
Open flick already searching for \fItitle\fR.
.TP
.B flick couch \fR[\fItitle\fR]
Watch a film together from two places. flick serves a room page, the play,
pause and seek sync, and the film itself from this computer through a
Cloudflare tunnel, and prints the room's link. The other person opens the link
in a desktop browser; nothing to install. Only files every browser plays (MP4
with H.264) are offered. Couch plays films, not shows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-engine " rqbit\fR|\fPwebtorrent"
The torrent engine. Default: rqbit if it is installed, else the built\-in
webtorrent.
.TP
.BI \-\-player " iina\fR|\fPmpv\fR|\fPvlc\fR|\fPbrowser"
The player. Default: the first one installed, in that order.
.TP
.B \-\-dub
Anime: prefer dual\-audio releases.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B type
Search films and shows.
.TP
.BR \(<- " " \(->
Move along the poster wall; change season on a show.
.TP
.BR \(ua " " \(da
Move through episodes and sources.
.TP
.B tab
Switch section: continue, now showing, shows.
.TP
.B enter
Open a title, an episode, or play a source.
.TP
.B c
Couch: copy the room link while a film is on.
.TP
.B esc
Back, clear the search, or return to the splash.
.TP
.B paste
A magnet link or info hash plays straight away.
.TP
.B ctrl\-c
Quit. The torrent, the room and the tunnel close with flick.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/flick/config.json
Settings: \fBengine\fR, \fBplayer\fR, \fBcacheGB\fR (default 10), \fBdub\fR,
and for couch \fBroom\fR, \fBtunnelToken\fR and \fBtunnelHost\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/flick/history.json
What you watched, for continue watching and the episode marks.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/flick/
Films (capped at \fBcacheGB\fR, least recently watched removed first),
subtitles and posters.
.SH COUCH ON A FIXED ADDRESS
By default a couch room gets a new random trycloudflare.com address each time.
For one address that never changes, create a named Cloudflare tunnel routed to
http://127.0.0.1:8765 and put its token and hostname in the config as
\fBtunnelToken\fR and \fBtunnelHost\fR. The token is a secret.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rqbit (1),
.BR mpv (1)
